@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title Teardown — what runs after the agent exits, how long each step may take, and what the run log keeps
' purpose: the steps proveo runs once the agent has exited, the ceiling on each, and the record each leaves in the run log
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/teardown_steps.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/teardown_steps_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (Run's deferred teardown, TeardownClone, PreserveClone, removeSandbox)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/pushed.go (sandboxReflog, reportPushedBranches)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/launch_receipt.go (retireSandbox's SaveState)
'   why this was needed ............. _spec/_plans/tui-responsiveness.puml (C2, C3)
'   the order it is delivered in .... _spec/_plans/tui-upgrades-delivery.puml
'   the earlier deadlines ........... _spec/internal/sbx/kit-lifecycle.puml (A HUNG TEARDOWN)
'   how a run's status is chosen .... _spec/internal/backend/exit-code.puml
'   what the clone carry does ....... _spec/internal/sbx/clone-workspace.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
' This file grows as the delivery plan's teardown slices land. Landed so far:
' T2 (step timing) and T1 (deadlines), both 2026-11-10.
'
' ── EVERY STEP LEAVES ONE LINE IN THE RUN LOG (T2) ─────────────────────────
' Before this, the run log stamped section headers only. A finished run could
' not say how long any teardown step took, so "typical" silence was unknown
' and only the ceilings were (tui-responsiveness.puml, C2).
' `step(name, fn)` runs fn and records its name, duration and outcome.
' `stepDo` is the same for a call that returns no error. The record goes to
' the run log through ui.Logf, as
'   step: <name> <duration> ok
'   step: <name> <duration> failed: <first line of the error>
' NOTHING REACHES THE TERMINAL. ui.Logf writes to the log's own printer and
' is a no-op when no log is open, so a run whose log failed to open records
' nothing; it does not fail.
' THE NAMES ARE CONSTANTS in teardown_steps.go, because the step list that
' later draws them (delivery plan, T6) reads the same names.
'   agent              the agent's own run, start to exit
'   stop wait          from the Ctrl+C dialog's remove answer to the sbx
'                      client exiting (bounded by stopWait, 30s)
'   credential check · clone mode · pushed branches · egress record ·
'   memory evidence    the five calls that open teardown
'   clone              the whole carry; its parts are logged under it:
'     clone/.env · clone/snapshot · clone/output · clone/branches · clone/spec
'   resume state · home config · remove sandbox
' A PARENT AND ITS PARTS ARE BOTH LOGGED. `clone` is the total; the parts add
' up to less than it, because the probes between them (`sbx ls`, the clone-mode
' probe inside PreserveClone) belong to the parent. A clone run starts up to 31
' subprocesses; one row per subprocess would bury the steps an operator names.
' PreserveClone also serves the retire path at run START, so a retired
' sandbox's carry logs the same `clone/…` rows there. That is why the prefix
' is `step:` and not `teardown:`.
' THE SINK IS AN ATOMIC POINTER. Tests swap it to read the steps; one test in
' the package runs in parallel and reaches carryClone.
'
' ── FOUR CALLS HAD NO DEADLINE; NOW EACH HAS ONE (T1) ──────────────────────
' kit-lifecycle.puml bounded the carry path on 2026-10-22 and left SaveState
' and teardown's `sbx rm` STILL OPEN. Two more were found unbounded on
' 2026-11-10: sandboxReflog and the pushed-branch `git fetch`.
' THE REFLOG READ RAN BEFORE THE CARRY. sbx.Exists answers true when `sbx ls`
' fails, so on a wedged daemon a clone run waited 10s for `sbx ls` and then
' started `sbx exec … git log -g` with no deadline. Teardown stopped there,
' printed nothing, and no work had reached home.
' All four now run through guestCommand / guestRun under guestExecDeadline
' (3m, the ceiling the Executor chose on 2026-10-22: "36s probe 3m others").
'   sandboxReflog           a timeout reads as "no reflog": no pushed-branch
'                           lines and no question
'   the pushed `git fetch`  a timeout prints `fetch failed` with the deadline
'   SaveState               teardown and retire pass guestRun; a timeout
'                           prints "resume state not preserved"
'   `sbx rm --force`        removeSandbox; a timeout prints the warning and a
'                           rescue line: check `sbx ls`, then `sbx rm --force
'                           <name>` once sbx answers
' NEVER AN AUTOMATIC SHIM KILL: killing the shim made the daemon respawn it and
' stall again (kit-lifecycle.puml).
' A REMOVAL THAT TIMES OUT MAY BE HALF-DONE. The rescue line says to look
' first, because the sandbox's state is unknown at that point.
' [Unverified] Whether 3m is generous or tight for a healthy `sbx rm` or state
' save. No finished run had per-step times before T2; the first logs with
' `step:` rows answer it.
' Nine host-local git and tar calls still have no deadline. They get one when
' teardown becomes named steps with a context (delivery plan, T3).
'
' Pinned by internal/backend/sandbox/teardown_steps_test.go:
'   TestAStepIsRecordedOnceWithItsNameDurationAndOutcome
'   TestAnUnsunkStepReachesNeitherTheTerminalNorAnUnopenedLog
'   TestTeardownCloneRecordsItsSubStepsInOrder
'   TestTeardownDeadlineEndsEveryGuestCallThatNeverAnswers
'   TestAHungReflogAsksNoPushedBranchQuestion

component "the agent exits" as EXIT <<app>>
component """step(name, fn)""\nname · duration · outcome" as STEP <<app>>
database "the run log\n""step: clone/snapshot 1.2s ok""" as LOG <<db>>
component "four guest or network calls\nunder ""guestExecDeadline"" (3m)" as BOUND <<app>>
component "**a wedged sbx daemon**\nhung teardown before the carry" as HANG <<error>>
component "the rescue line\n""sbx ls"", then ""sbx rm --force""" as RESCUE <<host>>

EXIT ARROW_MAIN STEP
STEP ARROW_MAIN LOG : one row per step
STEP ARROW_MAIN BOUND
HANG ARROW_ERROR BOUND : what the deadline ends
BOUND ARROW_OPTIONAL RESCUE : a removal that timed out

note bottom of LOG
  **The log, never the terminal.** A step row is
  for the next person reading a slow run. The
  operator's screen gets a step list later,
  drawn from the same names.
end note

note bottom of STEP
  **A parent and its parts.** ""clone"" is the
  whole carry; ""clone/snapshot"" is one part.
  Probes between parts count toward the
  parent, so the rows stay few.
end note

note bottom of HANG
  **It ran first, and unbounded.** The reflog
  read sits before the carry. With no deadline
  a wedged daemon stopped teardown silently,
  with the agent's work still in the sandbox.
end note

note bottom of RESCUE
  **Look before removing again.** A removal
  that hit its deadline may be half-done. The
  line names ""sbx ls"" first; proveo never
  kills the shim itself.
end note
@enduml
